    </decisions>
    <decisions>
        <name>Look_for_Repuestos_PA_or_Autos_Motos_Usados</name>
        <label>Look for Repuestos PA or Autos Motos Usados</label>
        <locationX>380</locationX>
        <locationY>323</locationY>
        <defaultConnector>
            <targetReference>Get_Cross_Duplicate_AutosMotosUsados</targetReference>
        </defaultConnector>
        <defaultConnectorLabel>autos motos usados</defaultConnectorLabel>
        <rules>
            <name>Repuesto_y_PA</name>
            <conditionLogic>or</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>$Record.Industry</leftValueReference>
                <operator>EqualTo</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <stringValue>Repuestos</stringValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>$Record.Industry</leftValueReference>
                <operator>EqualTo</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <stringValue>PA</stringValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Get_Cross_Duplicate_RepuestoPA</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>Repuesto y PA</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>
    <description>Business purpose: alerts (without blocking, per US-005) when a Lead shares contact data across DIFFERENT fields with another lead — combinations that native matching rules cannot evaluate (cross-field: new Email vs existing SecondaryEmail__c and vice versa, same for Phone/SecondaryPhone__c). When used: after save on Lead create, and on update when any of the four fields changes. How it alerts: Chatter post on the lead record plus a custom notification (DuplicateLeadAlert) to the owner when the owner is a user (queues are skipped). Blank values are replaced by a sentinel so they never match other blanks. Dependencies: fields SecondaryEmail__c and SecondaryPhone__c on Lead; CustomNotificationType DuplicateLeadAlert; Chatter enabled. Same-field duplicates remain covered by the native matching rules. Country considerations: alert texts in Spanish.</description>
    <environments>Default</environments>
    <formulas>
        <description>Chatter message with the full clickable link to the matching lead. Phone match is exact text; formatting differences are not normalized in this version.</description>
        <name>alertaTexto</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>&quot;Posible duplicado: este lead comparte email o teléfono (campos cruzados) con el lead \&quot;&quot; &amp; {!duplicateLead.Name} &amp; &quot;\&quot;. Revíselo antes de continuar: &quot; &amp; {!fBaseUrl} &amp; &quot;/lightning/r/Lead/&quot; &amp; {!duplicateLead.Id} &amp; &quot;/view&quot;</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <description>Notification body: no URL needed, clicking the notification opens the matching lead (targetId).</description>
        <name>alertaTextoNotificacion</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>&quot;Posible duplicado: este lead comparte email o teléfono (campos cruzados) con el lead \&quot;&quot; &amp; {!Get_Cross_Duplicate_AutosMotosUsados.Name} &amp; &quot;\&quot;. Haga clic en esta notificación para abrir el lead coincidente.&quot;</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <description>Org base URL derived from the API endpoint, so links work in any sandbox or production without hardcoding the domain.</description>
        <name>fBaseUrl</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>LEFT({!$Api.Partner_Server_URL_560}, FIND(&quot;/services&quot;, {!$Api.Partner_Server_URL_560}) - 1)</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <description>Sentinel keeps a blank value from matching other blanks in the cross lookup.</description>
        <name>fEmail</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>IF(ISBLANK({!$Record.Email}), &quot;##SIN-VALOR##&quot;, {!$Record.Email})</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <name>fMobPhone</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>IF(ISBLANK({!$Record.MobilePhone}), &quot;##SIN-VALOR##&quot;, {!$Record.MobilePhone})</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <description>Sentinel keeps a blank value from matching other blanks in the cross lookup.</description>
        <name>fPhone</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>IF(ISBLANK({!$Record.Phone}), &quot;##SIN-VALOR##&quot;, {!$Record.Phone})</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <description>Sentinel keeps a blank value from matching other blanks in the cross lookup.</description>
        <name>fSecEmail</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>IF(ISBLANK({!$Record.SecondaryEmail__c}), &quot;##SIN-VALOR##&quot;, {!$Record.SecondaryEmail__c})</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <description>Sentinel keeps a blank value from matching other blanks in the cross lookup.</description>
        <name>fSecPhone</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>IF(ISBLANK({!$Record.SecondaryPhone__c}), &quot;##SIN-VALOR##&quot;, {!$Record.SecondaryPhone__c})</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <description>Custom notifications only accept users as recipients; queue-owned leads skip the notification and keep the Chatter post.</description>
        <name>ownerEsUsuario</name>
        <dataType>Boolean</dataType>
        <expression>BEGINS({!$Record.OwnerId}, &quot;005&quot;)</expression>
    </formulas>
    <interviewLabel>Lead AS Cross Field Duplicate Alert {!$Flow.CurrentDateTime}</interviewLabel>
    <label>Lead AS Cross Field Duplicate Alert</label>
